{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297929-ex-3-lunars-prototype00-s-ess1-charm-picks","id":1297929,"title":"[Ex 3 Lunars] Prototype00's Ess1 Charm Picks.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-19T05:36:45-07:00","id":1297929,"title":"[Ex 3 Lunars] Prototype00's Ess1 Charm Picks.","content":"Hello Fellow Lunars fans, just thought I'd provide my top picks of Charms at Essence 1 (newbie character creation) and why, mechanically. Hopefully it sparks some neato characters in your next Lunars game.<br /> <br /> (Note: I am not a Mathematician by training, so this is basic stuff, so everyone should be good to go).<br /> <br /> <b>Universal:</b><br /> <br /> Hybrid Body Transformation (4m, Simple): There are two ways to view this Charm, either you are going to fight in it (in that case pack it with the nastiest combat stuff out there, like Wings, Unusual Hide, Deadly Natural Weapons e.t.c.) or you aren't (In which case you can build it with a sensory suite or a social suite), either way, a versatile choice.<br /> <br /> Quicksilver Second Face (2i, Reflexive): Pure gold for those who shapeshift into animals for combat, always be ready.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b><br /> <br /> Glance Oration Technique -&gt; Predator or Prey Mirror (3m, Reflexive): There are a bunch of Lunar Charms that are a lot nastier if you have a tie of Fear, P/P Mirror provides that without even to engage in Social Conflict.<br /> <br /> Glance Oration Technique -&gt; Perfect Symmetry (5m, Reflexive): Limit breaker for Appearance, I've always loved Pretty Kitty strats<br /> <br /> Feral Smile Tactic (3m Supplemental) -&gt; Is actually a great combat charm if you want to pull off the Predator's Menace Latent trick. Terrifying Beastial Visage (5m, Reflexive) if you want to go all out, but I feel it's gilding the lilly a bit.<br /> <br /> Subtle Silver Declaration ( - , Permanent) -&gt; Always useful, basically perfect disguise for your Tell. -&gt;Moon's Hidden Face (2m, Indefinite) and hide all your mutations too! Great for those who start with a Tell Mutation of Unusual Hide OOOOO<br /> <br /> <b>Charisma: </b><br /> <br /> Argent Songbird Voice (2m, Reflexive) - &gt; The other part to the Predator's Menace Latent Trick (affect all enemies without penalty) and also the ability to just buy successes with your Excellency is actually probably way better than anything Solars can do with 100% success.<br /> <br /> Poised Lion Attitude (3m, Reflexive) -&gt; See Predator's Menace. This is great because you can crash your enemies and attack right after.<br /> <br /> Pack Calling Cry (5m, +1WP, Simple) -&gt; Untamed Soul Unity - All the familiars, with time! Give your Solar Mate a Tyrant Lizard best bud/mount (wait, you can do that too.)<br /> <br /> <b>Dexterity: </b><br /> <br /> Emerald Grasshopper Form (10m 1wp, Simple) -&gt; The ultimate spying / stealth charm. Unless the enemy has 4+ successes it doesn't even have a chance to see you.<br /> <br /> Finding the Needle's Eye (3m, Supplemental) -&gt; Is okay, but is a requirement for Weapon Snatching Coils (5m, Supplemental) -&gt; Guess what, fellow Exalts, without that Goremaul, you are pretty boned against an &quot;unarmed&quot; Lunar.<br /> <br /> Sinuous Striking Grace (3m, Reflexive) -&gt; Effective +5 Successes on your JB roll is real good, and +1 non charm dice to attack is just gravy. Go-first is always strong.<br /> <br /> Agile Beast Defense (1m, Reflexive) -&gt; If your init is high (see Sinuous Striking Grace for how), +1 to all defences! (And if you are Death Kitty, you can decide after the attack roll is made!)<br /> <br /> Bending Before the Storm (2m, Reflexive) -&gt; Your Onslaught Negator, once again you need high Init.<br /> <br /> Golden Tiger Stance (3m, 2i, Reflexiv) -&gt; +1 more defence (no need for Initiative) and no Onslaught if enemies miss you!<br /> <br /> Coiled Serpent Strikes (3m, Reflexive) -&gt; For 3m, this is a big effect. Missed with your Decisive? No worries, here's another chance for you to wreck face.<br /> <br /> Swift Killer Style (1m, 2i, Supplemental) -&gt; If you are in a flying form, going straight up after your attack means that they probably can't attack you.<br /> <br /> Snake Finger Style (5m) -&gt; Endless uses! This is basically your get out of jail free ability (the double 9 is not so impressive, but you always operate as if you had equipment, I like that!)<br /> <br /> Oof, more than I expected, never fear, I shall reserve the rest for part the Second.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T06:53:54-07:00","id":1297946,"title":"","content":"Sinuous striking grace only lets the lunar act earlier in the round, it doesn't actually grant initiative. So its synergy with Agile beast defense is indirect (you can whither before they act), not direct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T07:22:51-07:00","id":1297951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297929-ex-3-lunars-prototype00-s-ess1-charm-picks?p=1297946#post1297946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sinuous striking grace only lets the lunar act earlier in the round, it doesn't actually grant initiative. So its synergy with Agile beast defense is indirect (you can whither before they act), not direct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. But Go First means you have a good chance to be King Initiative that round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T08:41:29-07:00","id":1297965,"title":"","content":"<b>Intelligence</b><br /> <br /> Memory Drinking Meditation (1m, Reflexive) -&gt; For when you really want to ghost a fella, this will tell you all you need to know about him and the people around him. (In fact, ghost a fella, and drink his memories about your actual Target and you might dig up some actionable dirt!)<br /> <br /> Inevitable Genius Insight (1m, Supplemental) -&gt; Use utter bullshit specialties from other abilities to justify Lore rolls. But it works as a good pre-req for -&gt; Wayfaring Sage Meditation (- , Permanent) -&gt; Pick some good Intimacies at Major (the more the merrier) and soon you'll be <i>swimming </i>in Lore specialties -&gt; Which works as a prereq and resets Dreaming Wisdom Revelation (7m, 1wp, Simple) -&gt; This is a <i><b>good</b></i> charm, I don't think I've even seen something as good on the Solar side. When you use it (every couple of days or so) just gun that Excellency and rack up the successes. Then reset it with the aforesaid good intimacies. Just immediately use it again and bank even more Foresight points, in prep for resetting it again. Muster a veritable mint of points that you can use to justify all sorts of bullshit, or just spam sorceries until the Shikari give up, up to you.<br /> <br /> Edit: Apparently this doesn\u2019t work because the Motes are commuted and when you use the Charm again, you de-commit the notes from the previous use. Still, having this pool is better than not having it.<br /> <br /> Penumbra Witch Mastery (3m, Supplemental) -&gt; Basically breaks up an Excellency so you can spend more from Peripheral and rerolls 1s. Excellency + Effect + spend more in Peripheral is always a winning combination in my book.<br /> <br /> Ironically, nothing in Sorcery (Apart from Terrestrial Circle, natch) is as good for shape sorcery as all these other Intelligence charms that I just mentioned.<br /> <br /> <b>Manipulation</b><br /> <br /> Inexplicable Mystery Incarnation (2m, Reflexive) -&gt; Mute all my mote expenditure for this massive social whammy I'm going to put on you? Don't mind if I do!<br /> <br /> Moonlight Curtain Drawn -&gt; Argent Deceiver Smile (5m, Reflexive): Is basically 5m for +3 Guile in an entire scene (Lunars always be lyin yo)<br /> <br /> <b>Perception</b><br /> <br /> Ever Wary Fox Technique (3m Reflexive) -&gt; Just generally useful, a free success against lurking ambushers (and should apply to Secret Sense Intuition!) traps, or when you are sleeping with no penalties whatsoever!<br /> <br /> Unwavering Predator's Eye ( - / Permanent) -&gt; Just dump Wits. Do it. Along with Arrogant Lion Bearing (-/Permanent) from Charisma which I forgot to mention, these charms remove Wits from 70 - 80% of it's applications.<br /> <br /> Secret Sense Intuition (3m, Reflexive) -&gt; Is probably my favorite charm in Perception. If you have a high Per+Socialize, and jack it up with Excellencies when the ST tells you that you can roll it, you should never be ambushed again. It gives you 2 chances vs any foe to notice them, and the attempts target guile then stealth. Not many enemies are going to have massive values in both against all your bennies. You can even do this against all kinds of ghosties and spirits with Perceiving the Hidden World (4m, Reflexive) without having to activate it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 03-19-2019, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T05:23:37-07:00","id":1298123,"title":"","content":"<b>Stamina</b><br /> <br /> Impenetrable Beast Armor (3m, Reflexive) -&gt; Is basically an excellency splitter for soak for the most part, allowing you to shunt three points of it into your Peripheral spend. Its also a pre-req for:<br /> <br /> Durant Quicksilver Adaptation (- / Permanent) -&gt; Is one of the best soak charms around, not because of how much it adds, but because it allows you to be super Mote efficient with your soak, baiting others into spending motes they shouldn't have to add threshold successes that you then casually soak up for a mote apiece.<br /> <br /> Steel Paw Style (- / permanent) -&gt; For DBT Dex deniers, this is the ultimate charm. Parry with how tough your face is!<br /> <br /> Ox Body Technique (- / permanent) -&gt; Lunar Ox Body is back! This was a meme in 2e, about how it was the best Ox body. And if you have 5 Sta, it is!<br /> <br /> Bear Sleep Technique (10m, Simple) -&gt; Halting the Scarlet Flow (6m, 1wp) -&gt; Man, Lunars get all the Wolverine stuff, but boy is it expensive!<br /> <br /> All Consuming Crucible (3m) -&gt; Actually this charm is circumstantial at best. But it's Chompy's Charm, so we all love it.<br /> <br /> <b>Strength</b><br /> <br /> Towering Beast Form (15m / 1wp) -&gt; You're 15m down and your mote drip is dead, but if you want to be a Kaiju form, this is it. Time to piledrive some Warstriders.<br /> <br /> Deadly Claw Blow (- / permanent) -&gt; Str's alternative to Sta for replacing Dex in battle. Great for DBT Lunars as they get to add Strength to everything!<br /> <br /> Tiger Claw Swat (2m, 2i) -&gt;Parry or Clash an enemy? Knock them back one range band and prone. This basically screws multi-attackers and gives you a nice little bonus next round when you go for the throat.<br /> <br /> Deadly Beastman Transformation (1m, 1wp, Simple) -&gt; Is just nuts. Its basically like three charms from Tiger Style put together. It, and all the charms associated with it are the best way (I believe) to fight for a Str/Sta based Full Moon.<br /> <br /> Claws of the Silver Moon (5m, 1wp) -&gt; Is just nuts as well. Did you know you could have a Hippo with 22L/10 overwhelming damage? Thats just disgusting!<br /> <br /> Angry Rhino Charge (-/Permanent) Ah, you'll need this as well to complete the dump-dex plan. This lets you rush foes with Str.<br /> <br /> <b>Wits (Is all about the Cache Charms, yo)</b><br /> <br /> Desert Basilisc Diadem -&gt; Radiant Basilisc Jewel both (- / permanent) -&gt; If your concept really needs a Hearthstone (Sorcerors and Hierophant's eye for example) accept no substitutes and grow it yourself. Just pay Hearthstone OO for a Steady one if you need to get a Dependent Greater Heartstone and you're ready to party! (Shape Sorceries from Long Range to Kill Satraps, I meant).<br /> <br /> Phew! Hope all those are helpful. I'm sure I missed a couple, so you can tell me where I went wrong. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 03-20-2019, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T05:37:47-07:00","id":1298125,"title":"","content":"Inevitable Genius Insight also has fun synergies with Rugged Beast Endurance. Rugged Beast Endure gives you Survival specialties for wherever you are, and Inevitable Genius Insight lets you use those specialties to introduce facts about the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T05:53:29-07:00","id":1298127,"title":"","content":"You definitely missed Ferocious Guardian Beast Stance, especially since you've already got Bending Before the Storm and Coiled Serpent Strikes there. It's War Lion Stance, and if you're in the habit of being a pestletail forcing enemies to attack you instead of any friends you have that aren't walking tanks is pretty neat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297929-ex-3-lunars-prototype00-s-ess1-charm-picks?p=1298123#post1298123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Claws of the Silver Moon (5m, 1wp) -&gt; Is just nuts as well. Did you know you could have a Hippo with 21L/10 overwhelming damage? Thats just disgusting!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is! But it's also E2.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm also not sold on Deadly Beastman. -1 Defenses that cant be mitigated in any way is a serious penalty, as is having to take a simple action and spending a willpower every fight you use it. As has been noted in your other thread some animal forms (IMO Cat, Hippo, Pestletail, and Hellboar stand out) are really, really strong, especially with the right protean charms, they're indefinite and you get them for free just for being a lunar. Animal forms are also less likely to freak people out than beastman is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 03-20-2019, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T07:44:27-07:00","id":1298142,"title":"","content":"You cant use martial arts in animal form, beastman is more worth it for martial artists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T08:04:27-07:00","id":1298144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297929-ex-3-lunars-prototype00-s-ess1-charm-picks?p=1298127#post1298127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animal forms are also less likely to freak people out than beastman is.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're employing Deadly Beastman Transformation, I think the time for consideration of other people's feelings has passed.<br /> <br /> {checks back}<br /> <br /> People are going to be less freaked out if they see you dealing with an enemy by turning into a river horse and grinding them into paste beneath your feet?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T09:01:02-07:00","id":1298155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Inevitable Genius Insight also has fun synergies with Rugged Beast Endurance. Rugged Beast Endure gives you Survival specialties for wherever you are, and Inevitable Genius Insight lets you use those specialties to introduce facts about the area.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Ah, right that's true and if any of them uphold your Major Intimacies, Bang! Dreaming Wisdom Revelation Reset.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You definitely missed Ferocious Guardian Beast Stance, especially since you've already got Bending Before the Storm and Coiled Serpent Strikes there. It's War Lion Stance, and if you're in the habit of being a pestletail forcing enemies to attack you instead of any friends you have that aren't walking tanks is pretty neat. </div> </div> </div>Its pretty good to be able to do, and seeing as how even talky or caster Lunars can just turn into a Pestletail and wreck face (just always max Brawl and Dex and you'll be fine) basically every Lunar could do this. A bit situational if the rest of your party are badasses though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is! But it's also E2. </div> </div> </div>Ah, indeed it is. All these treasures hidden at E2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: I'm also not sold on Deadly Beastman. -1 Defenses that cant be mitigated in any way is a serious penalty, as is having to take a simple action and spending a willpower every fight you use it. As has been noted in your other thread some animal forms (IMO Cat, Hippo, Pestletail, and Hellboar stand out) are really, really strong, especially with the right protean charms, they're indefinite and you get them for free just for being a lunar. Animal forms are also less likely to freak people out than beastman is. </div> </div> </div>See, as I mentioned, every Lunar can just turn into a ridiculous animal killing machine. Just max Dex and Brawl and you are basically as badass as you can be in these forms.<br /> <br /> With DBT, its a specific kind of build. My ideal is Str/Sta (because you can dump Dex) and then, yeah, maybe Martial arts (Tiger Tiger Stylist or Falcon Falcon Punch?) to fully benefit. The animal you can be a good-great combatant for minimal investment. DBT requires you to work for it, and is probably best for Full Moons. But you can do a lot of Str/Sta related stuff like Grappling and Regenerating in combat that a pure Dex Animal Form (because that is the most relevant stat for animals) wouldn't be able to.<br /> <br /> I guess you could run Str/Sta Animals too. But they don't contribute as much as to DBT.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People are going to be less freaked out if they see you dealing with an enemy by turning into a river horse and grinding them into paste beneath your feet? </div> </div> </div>I mean, make sure you were wearing someone else's face when you did it? If I was a Lunar, I'd just look like generic commoner A all the time (with 5 appearance, might be a hard sell, I admit.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T09:07:02-07:00","id":1298157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you're employing Deadly Beastman Transformation, I think the time for consideration of other people's feelings has passed.<br /> <br /> {checks back}<br /> <br /> People are going to be less freaked out if they see you dealing with an enemy by turning into a river horse and grinding them into paste beneath your feet?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, but if other people see a guy fighting a horse, they're going to be less freaked out than if they see a horse-man. I've used animal forms loads of times to infiltrate and then fight; if people don't see a transformation, they don't generally assume it's a Lunar.<br /> <br /> But I agree with you that transforming into an animal during combat is just as Lunar-ish as DBT.<br /> <br /> As to DBT generally... I think it's a good combat buff generally for martial artists if they have high strength, but not a One True Pick due to that -1. I have Strength 5 and Hybrid Body, but my 50 charms don't include DBT; I just found other charms more appealing. I may get it in future though.<br /> <br /> If you don't use MA it might still be good because you can activate a bunch of other buffs at the same time.<br /> <br /> But I don't think it's the auto-pick it was in 2nd edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-20-2019, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T11:09:36-07:00","id":1298169,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that Deadly Beastman Transformation also allows several other Charms that would otherwise be Simple to be activated reflexively, which can significantly cut down on the time it takes to get all of your ducks in order.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297929-ex-3-lunars-prototype00-s-ess1-charm-picks?p=1298157#post1298157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but if other people see a guy fighting a horse, they're going to be less freaked out than if they see a horse-man.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's two parts to that. One is that beastfolk are just a thing in the setting; depending on where one is, they might be a mistrusted, somewhat marginalized thing, but I'd presume that in most of the more cosmopolitan locations they're going to be assumed to be more exotic than &quot;dear God, what is this freak occurrence&quot;. I imagine that in Nexus, if folks see some asskicker with horse features who hasn't started glowing silver yet, they'll just assume that it's somebody from down south who got blessed or cursed by Hiparkes or something.<br /> <br /> The other is that, keeping in mind that people with animal features are a thing that exists in the setting and folks might become conditioned to their presence enough to find it unremarkable, the right animal can end up being a lot scarier. If a naturally aggressive one, those are kind of intrinsically terrifying, with the manner in which they move and the noises they make being really fearsome to see, and the impact they can have upon a human body rather unnerving.<br /> <br /> If not a naturally aggressive animal, then it acting in a manner completely out of character is liable to be uncanny and disturbing to see, a clear indication that something is wrong; at best, that the animal is carrying some kind of nasty disease.<br /> <br /> A horse-man can easily be a distant acquaintance. A horse that is fighting a person is one that is not employing its God-given talents and inclinations to <i>run away</i> from violence, and when it's apparent to anybody with basic familiarity with a horse that it's not only not acting like a horse, but is very deliberately trying to assault and trample people, that's going to stand out and be weird.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, river horse was just me being cute about the meaning of the term &quot;hippopotamus&quot;. Have you ever seen photos or footage of hippopotamus chasing after people? With those <i>teeth</i>? If people see that happening, they get to shelter or higher ground, because it is fucking terrifying. Those damn things kill more people on the Nile than the crocodiles do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 03-20-2019, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T11:15:51-07:00","id":1298170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297929-ex-3-lunars-prototype00-s-ess1-charm-picks?p=1298155#post1298155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, make sure you were wearing someone else's face when you did it? If I was a Lunar, I'd just look like generic commoner A all the time (with 5 appearance, might be a hard sell, I admit.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, make sure you look like someone else when you're doing what exactly?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T13:29:54-07:00","id":1298187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297929-ex-3-lunars-prototype00-s-ess1-charm-picks?p=1298155#post1298155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its pretty good to be able to do, and seeing as how even talky or caster Lunars can just turn into a Pestletail and wreck face (just always max Brawl and Dex and you'll be fine) basically every Lunar could do this. A bit situational if the rest of your party are badasses though.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience War Lion Stance effect is still good with badasses if one of them is an offensive focused badass (say a grappler that leaves himself vulnerable to other enemies while grappling) or if they both do it. Two tanks defending for eachother first means enemies can't pick which one of you they are targeting, secondly there's some amazing effects that only work with defend other. The dream team of Full Moon in hippo/pestletail/hellboar form with a Dawn mate melee supernal rider wearing Heartsbalm using Ferocious Guardian Beast and War Lion Stance on eachother is mental.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297929-ex-3-lunars-prototype00-s-ess1-charm-picks?p=1298155#post1298155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With DBT, its a specific kind of build. My ideal is Str/Sta (because you can dump Dex) and then, yeah, maybe Martial arts (Tiger Tiger Stylist or Falcon Falcon Punch?) to fully benefit. The animal you can be a good-great combatant for minimal investment. DBT requires you to work for it, and is probably best for Full Moons. But you can do a lot of Str/Sta related stuff like Grappling and Regenerating in combat that a pure Dex Animal Form (because that is the most relevant stat for animals) wouldn't be able to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dumping Dex is kind of shooting yourself in the foot still I think, you are going to want those Dex charms eventually, evasion is at times preferable to parry, and it's required for MAs like Snake and Single Point. Really Str 5/Dex 5/Sta 5 is what you are going to want either way you go (DBT or animal forms) if you want to be the best Full Moon you can be, and it's plenty achievable with Lunar prices.<br /> <br /> As for animal forms being great at minimal investment and then not having as good avenues for improvement, Protean effects are amazing. Later on there's also Constant Quicksilver Rearrangement which lets you abuse all the animal forms all the time, sneaking and dodging as a cat and mauling people as a hippo and getting protean effects on every charm you use.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ok I kind of take back what I've said about animal forms being to one-true way though I'm still not sold on Deadly Beastman, because I'm realising what can be done not if you enhance your Martial Arts attacks with Lunar charms, but if you enhance your Lunar charms with martial arts supplementals. Which gets broken in a hurry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 03-20-2019, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T16:40:49-07:00","id":1298218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297929-ex-3-lunars-prototype00-s-ess1-charm-picks?p=1298170#post1298170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, make sure you look like someone else when you're doing what exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>While you are changing into an animal. Walk around looking like Dockworker A right before you turn into a Hippo and macerate a Shikari. I'd never go around in my true face if I could help it (and it's the same mote commitment anyway, to shapeshift).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T00:13:28-07:00","id":1298279,"title":"","content":"Yes, but people are still going to call the Wyld Hunt, even if they can't identify you. They saw a shapeshifter, which could well be a moon-demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T00:27:28-07:00","id":1298280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297929-ex-3-lunars-prototype00-s-ess1-charm-picks?p=1298218#post1298218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While you are changing into an animal. Walk around looking like Dockworker A right before you turn into a Hippo and macerate a Shikari. I'd never go around in my true face if I could help it (and it's the same mote commitment anyway, to shapeshift).</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's a question of which form of shapeshifting assault will freak people out more, then your human appearance beforehand is somewhat irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T01:48:29-07:00","id":1298284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297929-ex-3-lunars-prototype00-s-ess1-charm-picks?p=1298279#post1298279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but people are still going to call the Wyld Hunt, even if they can't identify you. They saw a shapeshifter, which could well be a moon-demon.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it's a question of which form of shapeshifting assault will freak people out more, then your human appearance beforehand is somewhat irrelevant. </div> </div> </div>Sure, sure, all true. But by using someone else\u2019s mug and not flaring your anima/showing your Tell, you can just use another annonymous Strangers face and GTFO out of there and the Hunt will probably have a 1/Entire population chance of finding you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T03:37:46-07:00","id":1298289,"title":"","content":"This feels like one of those conversations in which recitation of basic facts gradually deviates from a point that was being made at the start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T07:39:40-07:00","id":1298323,"title":"","content":"A bit, but at least we're still talking about freaking people out, which was the original point. I've seen much worse on this forum. One of the other Lunar threads I'm not posting on, because I saw the current conversation and couldn't at all work out how it had started or what people's actual points were.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, sure, all true. But by using someone else\u2019s mug and not flaring your anima/showing your Tell, you can just use another annonymous Strangers face and GTFO out of there and the Hunt will probably have a 1/Entire population chance of finding you. </div> </div> </div>Yes, and there are circumstances where you might want to do that.<br /> <br /> But<br /> a)when trying to affect a society, you probably don't want the Wyld Hunt turning up at all. They'll interfere with what you're doing, you'll constantly have to worry about them, and you won't be able to operate with impunity. In one game I play, we've managed to avoid having the Wyld Hunt turn up at all in the kingdom we live in, which is nice and relaxing.<br /> b)not all Lunars have the forms to use anyway.<br /> In the Essence 5 game I play, neither Lunar PC has any additional human forms.<br /> In the Lunar game I'm preparing to run, 4 players have sent me sheets so far, and none has any additional forms.<br /> Admittedly, in the other game (Essence 4) I play, the Changing Moon has a bunch of human forms (my Lunar just had one, his Solar Mate's... don't really want to implicate him anyway!). But she's Appearance 5-8, so too vain to travel as anyone else most of the time. Sometimes she pretends to be my Solar Mate because he keeps skipping meetings with the Pharoah and she needs to cover for him. (His shape goes around a lot...)<br /> <br /> I mean, it's a good idea at times. Worth considering. Just not really something you may be able to do, or find useful.<br /> <br /> Whereas no one calls the Wyld Hunt on a bear who's just, you know, being a bear.<br /> (And that's how I infiltrated the Pharoah's court!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T10:14:06-07:00","id":1298357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297929-ex-3-lunars-prototype00-s-ess1-charm-picks?p=1298323#post1298323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">b)not all Lunars have the forms to use anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar shapeshifting is the one thing in the game where I would adopt an attitude contrary to this. It is a thing that I think is so central to their characterisation and so casually acquired that a Lunar who never gets any of them is more of an aberration. It's not like playing a Solar where you didn't buy Larceny Charms just for the sake of reducing bondage or confinement as effective means of stopping you, and don't treat the potential to develop those Charms and their minimums as though they're as easy as they are in the system; if one is not playing somebody that is supposed to be very fresh, it strikes me as closer to a Flaw than anything.<br /> <br /> Mind, that's an attitude informed by the current Edition; I can imagine somebody working from some prior assumptions treating the sacred hunt as an inconvenience, or not wanting to purchase the knack to become able to undertake the inconvenience of the sacred hunt for humans.<br /> <br /> In this Edition, though? A Lunar has no excuse not to have some forms to use. It's not a skill that a character may plausibly have not been inclined to develop, it's like walking upr-<br /> <br /> \u2026.<br /> <br /> There are personalities and cultural backgrounds that would view even the default sacred hunt as applied to animals to not be conscionable, and even the most accommodating Heart's Blood Charms as demanding either more effort than they'd often be willing to put in or having no stomach for what they entail even if it doesn't consist of murder. Luna's diverse proclivities and more embracing attitude precludes any argument to the effect that people distinctly averse to the sacred hunt in any of its incarnations would be kind of excluded from the short list.<br /> <br /> Darn it, I hate it when that happens.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T11:00:58-07:00","id":1298361,"title":"","content":"You had me going for a while there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T11:09:26-07:00","id":1298366,"title":"","content":"You seem to have covered both sides adequately, so there's not much for me to say in terms of theory.<br /> <br /> For the sake of from-play examples (I like from-play examples):<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Currently I'm playing Dr Soma. She's Casteless, and hasn't been a Lunar that long. She's not eaten anyone yet, because... well, she's only killed a few people since Exalting, and they ambushed her (so Sacred Hunt doesn't work). And hunting someone to kill and eat them seems quite dishonourable.<br /> She may challenge someone to a kung-fu duel and, if they fight with honour and are worthy of respect, learn their form. But so far no-one seems interested in a friendly duel.<br /> <br /> She's in the same game as Timid Silk Blossom, a gentle rabbit-totem beauty who definitely wouldn't engage in such savage practices as cannibalism. (Assassination, killing prisoners, killing old men who happen to be in her way, running an Inquisition... sure. But not cannibalism.)<br /> <br /> <br /> In the other game I play, the Changing Moon has a whole heap of forms; a little girl, an old woman, an Emperor, her husband a Night Caste pauper-turned-prince, and loads of fat merchants. A few she got from sex, but most she just ate. We never asked why she'd eaten a little girl. Best not to.<br /> But she hasn't gone round murdering people for, what, a year or two? Since she became a mother. I think she's settled down.<br /> <br /> My own No Moon (currently on a trip since the edition charged; possibly he'll return now he has rules, but I have another character) had a few non-animal forms: the Changing Moon's Night Caste husband (his Solar Mate), an Emperor, and his girlfriend. I mean, he wasn't perfect, but he wouldn't just murder someone for power. That's morally wrong.<br /> Though he absolutely would murder and eat his identical twin/creator. But having the form of your identical twin is not very useful.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the person in that game most likely to commit murder is my Zenith. Last session I tried repeatedly to kill a ghost spymaster smuggling evil artefacts for an oblivion cult, and the other PC there, an Immaculate Monk, wouldn't let. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> As to the characters I've been sent for my game... well, they're all pretty new Lunars, half of them don't even have a Caste. Maybe some of them would eat a human for their form, but haven't had the opportunity (or merit points!).<br /> One guy has brought the charm to gain the form of those who break sanctified oaths to him, but mostly so he could get the upgrade to curse people with plagues of toads (as he's a toad-shaman). No-one else has bothered to get any charms for gaining more human forms. They seem more interested in mighty (or stealthy) animal forms. We'll see how the game progresses.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I think a lot of Lunars will have multiple human forms, especially as they get older, but there are reasons they might not, or might only have a few like my No Moon. And if you only have 2-3 forms, it's not such a perfect disguise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-21-2019, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T12:59:21-07:00","id":1298384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FODOR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297929-ex-3-lunars-prototype00-s-ess1-charm-picks?p=1298361#post1298361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You had me going for a while there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get me wrong, I wasn't writing that post theatrically; I was making the argument in the first half genuinely, as it is a perspective I have had in prior discussions. It was just that halfway through the counterargument struck me, and I could hardly leave it aside. Having the full text certainly has helped to overturn some of my own more firmly developed ideas about the Lunar Exalted, and I am all for that.<br /> <br /> That I kept the post at all was a combination of my being loathe to drop something once I have invested energy into making it, and a certain show of contrition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T06:12:43-07:00","id":1299189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297929-ex-3-lunars-prototype00-s-ess1-charm-picks?p=1298123#post1298123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Desert Basilisc Diadem -&gt; Radiant Basilisc Jewel both (- / permanent) -&gt; If your concept really needs a Hearthstone (Sorcerors and Hierophant's eye for example) accept no substitutes and grow it yourself. Just pay Hearthstone OO for a Steady one if you need to get a Dependent Greater Heartstone and you're ready to party! (Shape Sorceries from Long Range to Kill Satraps, I meant).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey I just realised with this you can pay the out-of-combat cost of being a T-Rex or Elephant and still recover motes, since you're always gaining +4m per hour as if in a four dot manse. Being a giant animal is perhaps still not always super practical, but its kind of nice if you want to be that guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T06:29:07-07:00","id":1299193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297929-ex-3-lunars-prototype00-s-ess1-charm-picks?p=1299189#post1299189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey I just realised with this you can pay the out-of-combat cost of being a T-Rex or Elephant and still recover motes, since you're always gaining +4m per hour as if in a four dot manse. Being a giant animal is perhaps still not always super practical, but its kind of nice if you want to be that guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed true, you can hang out as a T-Rex or Elephant and get a mote drip which is nice. (You also have a boulder sized magic rock in your forehead, but hey, thats part of the aesthetic)<br /> <br /> I'm right now thinking of what Ess 2 charms are super key both for combat/social as if you don't need a Greater Hearthstone for Shape Sorcery, you can pick up the Glory stone and cheat yourself an ESS 2 charm at character creation.<br /> <br /> But which one...? Claws of the Silver Moon for Killer Hippo of course, but I'm sure there are other choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T08:05:54-07:00","id":1299601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297929-ex-3-lunars-prototype00-s-ess1-charm-picks?p=1299193#post1299193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But which one...? Claws of the Silver Moon for Killer Hippo of course, but I'm sure there are other choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Single Point, Righteous Devil, or Crane Form if you're going MA for sure.<br /> <br /> Instinctive Supremacy Approach also aint bad, everyone likes free full excellencies.<br /> <br /> At E2 Heron Sheds Rain/Flowing Body Evasion seem the obvious picks for E3 combat charms, but possibly Red Visions Realized (roll join battle twice, very nice if you're a single point stylist) could be even better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 03-25-2019, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T21:44:15-07:00","id":1301225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297929-ex-3-lunars-prototype00-s-ess1-charm-picks?p=1297965#post1297965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Intelligence</b><br /> Penumbra Witch Mastery (3m, Supplemental) -&gt; Basically breaks up an Excellency so you can spend more from Peripheral and rerolls 1s. Excellency + Effect + spend more in Peripheral is always a winning combination in my book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Waitaminute.<br /> <br /> That's legit? O.o<br /> <br /> I mean, on a single action you can split your essence expenditure if it comes from multiple charms? Damn. Never thought about that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>French Exalt &amp; ST &amp; ToolMaker [<a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/\" target=\"_blank\">Website</a>]<br /> Advanced Character Generator <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1087290-advanced-character-generator#post1087290\" target=\"_blank\">Thread, </a><a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/exalted3/Fiche%20perso%20colab.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Excel Version</a> &amp; <a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/exalted3/Fiche%20perso%20colab.ods\" target=\"_blank\">LibreOffice Version</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141199-exalted-3-familiar-generator\" target=\"_blank\">Familiar Generator Thread</a> &amp; <a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/exalted3/Familiar%20Generator.ods\" target=\"_blank\">Libreoffice Version</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13355-refhi","name":"Refhi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13355_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T22:26:49-07:00","id":1301232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Refhi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297929-ex-3-lunars-prototype00-s-ess1-charm-picks?p=1301225#post1301225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Waitaminute.<br /> <br /> That's legit? O.o<br /> <br /> I mean, on a single action you can split your essence expenditure if it comes from multiple charms? Damn. Never thought about that...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, for each charm (Including Stat Excellency) you get to decide whether you spend the whole mote cost from Peripheral or Personal.<br /> <br /> What Penumbra does is it allows you to draw on your Peripheral for Charm costs and spend the rest of your motes from Personal up to your cap. (Normally you\u2019d have to draw on one pool fully for the Excellency)<br /> <br /> A useful savings.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also keep an eye out for Reflexive Scenelong Charms. Those all count as activation in their own instant (according to Vance), so as long as they cost 4 or less motes, you can activate as many of them at once from your peripheral pool and still not flare anima.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 03-31-2019, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}